#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

context="You have workflow skills for software development available in this project.

## Available Workflow Skills

/mission-architect — New projects: discover vision, output mission statement to thoughts/shared/missions/. Use before /specifier. Also takes a new subsystem inside an existing codebase when it has its own value proposition AND needs several parallel streams — then its mission must record the host system as a constraint.
/feature-architect — Brownfield features: define new feature in existing system, output feature brief to thoughts/shared/features/. Use before /fact-finder — brownfield skips /epic-planner, which exists to cut a whole spec into several streams. A feature needing that decomposition is a subsystem: send it to /mission-architect, never straight to /specifier.
/change-architect — Small changes, bug fixes, and maintenance work: record the intended target state, output change brief to thoughts/shared/changes/. Use before /fact-finder or /just-do-it depending on the brief's route: field (full → /fact-finder, direct → /just-do-it). A change needing more than one intended outcome belongs to /feature-architect.
/specifier — Transform mission statement into technical spec. Output to thoughts/shared/specs/. Use after /mission-architect.
/epic-planner — Decompose spec into epics. Output to thoughts/shared/epics/. Use after /specifier.
/fact-finder — Map the codebase for a spec or question. Spawns codebase agents for isolation. Output to thoughts/shared/facts/. Requires a target artifact upstream. Use before /planner — /planner refuses a plan from a facts report without one.
/planner — Write a sequenced, evidence-based implementation plan. Output to thoughts/shared/plans/. Use after /fact-finder.
/implement — Execute a plan wave-by-wave via concurrent subagents, with one combined spec-and-quality review gate per task. Use after /planner.
/just-do-it — Execute a route: direct change brief directly — no fact report, no plan; one reviewer, one commit, one record. Use after /change-architect when the brief carries route: direct.
/prototype — Optional. Spike a rough idea into disposable code in an isolated worktree and reach a go/no-go decision. Use before /mission-architect, /feature-architect or /change-architect, when it is not yet clear whether the thing should be built at all.

## Workflow Ordering

Greenfield:  /mission-architect → /specifier → /epic-planner → /fact-finder → /planner → /implement
Brownfield:  /feature-architect → /fact-finder → /planner → /implement
Subsystem:   own value proposition AND several parallel streams → take the greenfield path, mission records the host system as a constraint (either condition alone stays brownfield)
Small fix:   /change-architect → (/fact-finder → /planner → /implement | /just-do-it)
Unsure:      /prototype → then one of the four above, on a 'go' decision

## Rules

- Always run /fact-finder before /planner — planner needs a verified research report.
- Every workflow route begins with a target artifact upstream of /fact-finder. /planner refuses a plan from a facts report with upstream-artifact none, unless QA-sourced.
- Always run /planner before /implement — /implement needs a plan file.
- /just-do-it runs only on a brief carrying route: direct.
- Invoke skills proactively when the user's request matches the trigger condition.
- When the user says 'research X', 'understand X', or 'investigate X' → invoke /fact-finder.
- When the user says 'implement', 'build', or 'execute the plan' → invoke /implement."

escape_for_json() {
    local s="$1"
    s="${s//\\/\\\\}"
    s="${s//\"/\\\"}"
    s="${s//$'\n'/\\n}"
    s="${s//$'\r'/\\r}"
    s="${s//$'\t'/\\t}"
    printf '%s' "$s"
}

escaped=$(escape_for_json "$context")

printf '{\n  "hookSpecificOutput": {\n    "hookEventName": "SessionStart",\n    "additionalContext": "%s"\n  }\n}\n' "$escaped"
